  "question": {
    "text": "A normal line with positive direction cosines to the plane <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> makes equal angles with the coordinate axes. The distance of the point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from the line <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> measured parallel to the plane <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "VQhPp",
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn></math> units",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "X0dkv",
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></math> units",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BQZz3",
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></math> units",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "kFsTa",
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math> units",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/dd55fd7d-4a21-40f5-b864-e345891dab33.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.30694in;height:1.4in\" /></p><p>Direction ratios of the normal to the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1,1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#62;</mo></math><br />Any general point on the&nbsp;given line is&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2,2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />From the diagram<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4,2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>.</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />So, coordinates of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,5</mo></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Hence,&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units</p>",
